<Layout title="Terms" description="The terms for buying and using Art of Small Steps courses and products, and for using artofsmallsteps.com.">
  <article class="legal">
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 23 November 2026</p>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="lede">These are the terms for buying any Art of Small Steps course or product, and for using artofsmallsteps.com. I've tried to keep them short and in plain English. If anything is unclear, write to me and I'll explain.</p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>Art of Small Steps, its courses and products are created by Sophie Kemenes. The business behind them is:</p>
    <p class="seller">
      Kemenes György Lászlóné, egyéni vállalkozó (a Hungarian sole trader), trading as Art of Small Steps<br />
      Tímár u. 19/J, 1034 Budapest, Hungary<br />
      Hungarian tax number: 92558515-1-41<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:hello@artofsmallsteps.com">hello@artofsmallsteps.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>In these terms, "we", "us" and "I" mean this business, and "you" means the person buying or using one of our products.</p>

    <h2>2. What you're buying</h2>
    <p>Each product has its own page on this website. That page tells you what's included, how and when it's delivered, and the price. <strong>The description on the product page at the moment you buy is part of your contract with us</strong>, together with these terms. If we change a product page later, the version you saw when you bought still applies to you.</p>
    <p>Our products are digital: for example courses delivered by email, workbooks as PDF, and audio or video material. Unless the product page says otherwise, everything you receive is yours to keep, with no login, subscription or expiry date.</p>

    <h2>3. Delivery</h2>
    <p>Right after you buy, you'll get a confirmation email. Delivery then follows the schedule on the product page. Some courses start on a fixed date, and if you buy before then, the first part arrives on that date.</p>
    <p>The emails come from Art of Small Steps through our email provider. If something hasn't arrived, please check your spam or promotions folder first, then write to me and I'll send it again.</p>

    <h2>4. Price and payment</h2>
    <p>Prices are shown on the product page in pounds sterling (GBP) and include VAT where it applies. You pay the price shown at the moment you buy. Some products have a launch or early price for a limited time, and the product page says until when. Our products are currently sold to customers in the United Kingdom.</p>
    <p>Orders are processed by <strong>Stripe</strong>, through its Link service, which acts as the reseller (the "merchant of record") for your purchase. This means Stripe takes the payment, handles VAT, and sends you your receipt and invoice. Your card statement will show <strong>LINK.COM*</strong> followed by our name. Stripe's own terms apply to the payment itself. We never see or store your card details.</p>
    <p>The contract for the product itself, meaning what you receive and how it is delivered, is with us, and we are responsible for it.</p>

    <h2>5. Your money back</h2>
    <p>For every product, you can ask for a full refund within <strong>14 days of buying</strong>, for any reason or none, even if you've already opened or used it. You also keep your statutory rights. The details are in the <a href="/refund/">Refund policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>6. What our products are, and what they aren't</h2>
    <p>Our courses and products are self-reflection and self-development tools: exercises, questions and stories to help you look at your life from a new angle and choose your next small steps.</p>
    <p><strong>They are not therapy, counselling, coaching tailored to you, or medical or psychological advice</strong>, and they don't replace them. If you're going through a crisis, or struggling with your mental health, please speak to your GP or a qualified professional. In the UK you can call Samaritans free, day or night, on 116 123, or NHS 111.</p>
    <p>You take part at your own pace and in your own way, and you decide what to do with what you discover. We can't promise any particular result, because the work and the choices are yours.</p>

    <h2>7. Using the material</h2>
    <p>Our lessons, workbooks, audio, videos and illustrations are protected by copyright and belong to us. Buying a product gives you a personal licence to use it for yourself. Please don't resell, share, publish or forward the material, or use it to teach others, without asking first. Quoting a line or two with credit is always fine.</p>
    <p>If you'd like to give one of our products to someone else, you're very welcome to buy it for them.</p>

    <h2>8. If something goes wrong</h2>
    <p>If a product isn't as described, or something doesn't arrive or doesn't work, tell me and I'll put it right. If I can't, you're entitled to a refund under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 as well as under our own 14-day promise.</p>
    <p>Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that can't be limited by law. Otherwise, our total liability to you is limited to the price you paid. We aren't responsible for losses that weren't foreseeable, or for business losses: our products are for personal use.</p>
    <p>If a schedule ever has to change, for example because of illness or a technical problem, I'll let you know by email as soon as I can, and you'll still receive everything you paid for.</p>

    <h2>9. Notes on individual products</h2>
    <p>Where a product works differently from the general terms above, it's noted here.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>RECHART: The Wayfinder Method</strong> sets off on Sunday 3 January 2027. If you buy before then, you'll receive the preparation emails in the meantime and the first lesson on 3 January. If you buy on or after that date, the lessons start straight away.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. The website</h2>
    <p>You're welcome to read and share the free content on artofsmallsteps.com. Please don't copy it wholesale or present it as your own. We try to keep the site accurate and available, but can't promise it will always be uninterrupted or error-free. How we handle your personal data is described in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> and the <a href="/cookies/">Cookie policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version that applies to your purchase is the one on this page when you bought.</p>

    <h2>12. Law and disputes</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by Hungarian law. If you live in the United Kingdom, this doesn't take away any of the protections you have under the law where you live, and you can bring a claim in your local courts. If you have a complaint, please write to me first at <a href="mailto:hello@artofsmallsteps.com">hello@artofsmallsteps.com</a>. I read every message myself and will do my best to sort it out quickly and fairly.</p>
